# Committed on purpose, and it holds no secret.
#
# `$env/static/public` is resolved at build time from whatever exists then, and
# importing a name it does not export is a hard build failure — so a variable
# that is only ever set in a deployment dashboard breaks every local checkout
# and every CI run. This file is the declaration that the variable exists; the
# empty value is the off switch.
#
# Precedence, which is what makes an empty default safe: Vite's `loadEnv` reads
# the `.env` files first and then copies `process.env` over the top, so a real
# value injected by the host (Vercel's project settings) wins here, and
# `.env.local` — gitignored — wins locally.

# Google Analytics 4 measurement id, e.g. G-XXXXXXXXXX. Set it in the Vercel
# project rather than here. Unset, `analytics.svelte` renders nothing at all:
# no Partytown, no gtag, no beacon. See src/lib/analytics/gtag.ts.
PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=
